    "created_at": "2026-03-27T19:28:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-27T19:28:03Z",
    "body": "Concretely it would be anything which uses the WebIDL resolve steps. The problem isn't so much that the IDL is actively 'wrong' so much as it is that it's very easy for implementations to not realize that resolving a promise runs script basically any time. \n\nIf we made this change we actually could guarantee that resolving a promise never ran script at the cost of -some- promise reactions happening in later ticks. ",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
